  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1225 AM CST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nNot much change in the forecast from the previous issuance. Will \nexpect a surface low to meander in the northern Gulf allowing for \npersistent northeasterly flow. Our next cold front is expected to \nsweep through the region this weekend with a reinforcing surge of \nhigh pressure behind it. This will allow for cooler temperatures to \nremain through the end of next week. Low to medium rain chances \n(30-65%) are warranted along the front as it moves through South \nTexas Sunday.\n\nMinor coastal flooding will remain a threat tonight into Saturday \ndue to northeasterly flow and long period swells. Seas will \ngradually subside as a broad surface low, that has influenced the\nthe Gulf waters, is expected to get picked up by our next front \nSunday.",
